{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":".github/workflows/ci.yml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T06:21:31.835071Z","id":"b0f1d8ab693a9733f308ebd6cccae0068f42363f9bcf97ecb0d724b404fa7bc0","body":{"detail":"CI's worker job runs scripts/check-wasm.sh and just worker-test natively, outside scripts/bazel-test.sh --ci, so just ci stays Bazel-only and makes no target/ or node_modules in a worktree. Under Bazel it would need a wasm32-unknown-unknown platform for rules_rust, a C toolchain whose clang targets wasm32 for bundled SQLite (rusqlite's sqlite-wasm-rs), crates/clax-worker's own Cargo.lock in crate_universe, worker-build (crates/clax-worker/build.sh installs it with cargo install) and wrangler from npm. Until then a local just ci does not run them; just check-wasm and just worker-test do.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":81},"end":{"line":117},"content_hash":"f75be890b6096e95cba144280fc77498d29f12bed337bdff3b9c0e486005b53e"},"summary":"Build crates/clax-worker and check the Worker's crates for wasm32 under Bazel","tags":["build","ci","revisit:rules_rust builds a wasm32 target with a C toolchain here, or a wasm32 break reaches main past the worker job","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":".github/workflows/ci.yml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T20:36:33.910414Z","id":"38985b9c78838e41be333a059185193c8479f029c7b59b504b5f6175c8cad1cf","body":{"detail":"CI's worker job runs scripts/check-wasm.sh and just worker-test natively, outside scripts/bazel-test.sh --ci, so just ci stays Bazel-only and makes no target/ or node_modules in a worktree. Under Bazel it would need a wasm32-unknown-unknown platform for rules_rust, a C toolchain whose clang targets wasm32 for bundled SQLite (rusqlite's sqlite-wasm-rs), crates/clax-worker's own Cargo.lock in crate_universe, worker-build (crates/clax-worker/build.sh installs it with cargo install) and wrangler from npm. Until then a local just ci does not run them; just check-wasm and just worker-test do.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":81},"end":{"line":119},"content_hash":"62cd0c2a7a506af02bc95d2e2b3d3f415b7b4811c74ea0183bd34e08aa55b1e9"},"summary":"Build crates/clax-worker and check the Worker's crates for wasm32 under Bazel","supersedes":"b0f1d8ab693a9733f308ebd6cccae0068f42363f9bcf97ecb0d724b404fa7bc0","tags":["build","ci","revisit:rules_rust builds a wasm32 target with a C toolchain here, or a wasm32 break reaches main past the worker job","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":".github/workflows/ci.yml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T20:36:33.972449Z","id":"c62c963e7d79bef354f0611d2b1bffbc1499018245c6dc902126cf2613e2ccd3","body":{"detail":"web/BUILD.bazel declares //web:playwright with the @playwright/test package's generated playwright_binary, replacing a js_binary whose entry point inside the linked package failed analysis on every platform (\"is a prefix of the other\", CI run 39153903425). On macOS it builds and `bazelisk run //web:playwright -- --version` prints Version 1.63.0, and scripts/bazel-test.sh --ci now builds it. install-deps itself installs Chromium's system libraries with apt through sudo, which only the ubuntu-latest runner does; the first CI run of this workflow shows whether it works there.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":33},"end":{"line":36},"content_hash":"2e92564feb69742457763f8603190b484513b992dfce20a47e06c9bb9e1111bd"},"summary":"`bazelisk run //web:playwright -- install-deps chromium` has not run on the Linux runner since //web:playwright became rules_js's playwright_binary","tags":["ci","bazel","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":".github/workflows/publish-pi.yml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:03:55.566044Z","id":"d8862507094b924f83798d71c52fd21afc4efebf7e999671e0316e185dae4882","body":{"detail":"Failure: a user with write access pushes a branch whose publish-pi.yml drops this step (or checks out any commit) and runs `gh workflow run publish-pi.yml --ref that-branch -f dry_run=false`; workflow_dispatch runs the workflow file at that ref (https://docs.github.com/en/actions/writing-workflows/choosing-what-your-workflow-does/events-that-trigger-workflows#workflow_dispatch), the job gets an OIDC token (id-token: write), and npm accepts it because a trusted publisher configured as scripts/release.sh:678-681 and docs/usage.md print it ('no environment') matches on repository and workflow filename only. The check guards against mistakes, not against an unreviewed commit being published.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":61},"end":{"line":80},"content_hash":"8cb5391f3658c557a7e10550b0a97d7202f73e75328c272f5542ee6a447974b0"},"suggested_fix":"Give the publish job a GitHub environment (e.g. npm) whose deployment branches allow only main, and print/document that environment for the npm trusted-publisher setup, so npm refuses tokens from runs on other refs.","summary":"The on-main and CI-passed check is bypassable by anyone who can dispatch: the workflow runs from the dispatched ref, and the trusted publisher names no environment","tags":["review","review:release-script-2","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":".github/workflows/publish-pi.yml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:03:55.566070Z","id":"f98bbcc12e690b22ab75a2ab1ca1b48e45c5d5016f01b899fad51d373251f7de","body":{"detail":"Failure: on a push to main, ci.yml's perf-log job (.github/workflows/ci.yml:125-134) joins concurrency group perf-log; when a third push queues behind a running one, GitHub cancels the pending one (https://docs.github.com/en/actions/writing-workflows/choosing-what-your-workflow-does/control-the-concurrency-of-workflows-and-jobs), so the release's pin or merge commit gets conclusion 'cancelled' though its bazel gate passed. This step then refuses the publish, and scripts/release.sh:622-627 (step 13) fails the same way; even uncancelled, step 13 waits for the benchmarks (timeout 60 min each, queued behind earlier ones) within its 90-minute poll budget.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":75},"end":{"line":80},"content_hash":"ddb39cd4f10ec443d61e1d88e90da05962df7d7748990f346ab37a5b21d4b656"},"suggested_fix":"Judge the bazel job's conclusion (gh run view <id> --json jobs) rather than the run's, in both this check and release.sh's step 13 wait.","summary":"'CI passed' is the whole ci.yml run's conclusion, which includes the perf-log job: a cancelled perf run refuses the publish","tags":["review","review:release-script-2","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":".github/workflows/publish-pi.yml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:05:39.188902Z","id":"51e747beb589c25b3828bd3bbc9733b42916715b53575dcb99042fcb35e7dc06","body":{"detail":".github/workflows/publish-pi.yml:22-32 triggers on workflow_dispatch only; :46-56 gives the publish job id-token: write and no `environment:`. scripts/release.sh:678-681 prints the trusted-publisher setup with 'no environment'. workflow_dispatch runs the workflow file from the chosen ref (https://docs.github.com/en/actions/writing-workflows/choosing-what-your-workflow-does/events-that-trigger-workflows#workflow_dispatch), and npm's trusted publisher matches on owner, repository, workflow filename and an optional environment (https://docs.npmjs.com/trusted-publishers), so a branch copy of publish-pi.yml without the check at :61-80 can publish. Kind concern is right: it takes someone with write access.","kind":"comment","references":"d8862507094b924f83798d71c52fd21afc4efebf7e999671e0316e185dae4882","summary":"confirmed: the on-main/CI check lives in the dispatched ref's workflow file, and the job has no environment to bind the trusted publisher to main","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":".github/workflows/publish-pi.yml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:05:39.189046Z","id":"b89c1558e03b947a7f40d9381f82f22c41cbc38ed4ccc6b355d380127e7f3838","body":{"detail":".github/workflows/publish-pi.yml:75-80 requires `.[0].conclusion == success` for the ci.yml push run. scripts/release.sh:622-627 (step_13) waits via await_run, which accepts only 'completed success' (scripts/release.sh:529-534). .github/workflows/ci.yml:126-140 adds perf-log on pushes to main (needs: bazel, timeout-minutes: 60, concurrency group perf-log, cancel-in-progress: false). GitHub cancels an already pending job in a concurrency group when another queues, whatever cancel-in-progress says (https://docs.github.com/en/actions/writing-workflows/choosing-what-your-workflow-does/control-the-concurrency-of-workflows-and-jobs), so the run concludes 'cancelled' and both gates refuse.","kind":"comment","references":"f98bbcc12e690b22ab75a2ab1ca1b48e45c5d5016f01b899fad51d373251f7de","summary":"confirmed: both gates read the whole ci.yml run's conclusion, which includes the perf-log job","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":".github/workflows/publish-pi.yml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:21:06.112364Z","id":"02977601a148bea47a5f8902ae7901801aba6ca36c690a53dde002d549c853a6","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:d4f3ff246","summary":"publish-pi.yml's job runs in the GitHub environment npm, which the trusted publisher names (release.sh's printed setup, docs/usage.md and the workflow header now say environment npm); release.sh reads the environment read-only and warns in a dry run, refuses a release, when it is missing or allows more than main, printing the settings to make. Evidence: //scripts:release_script PASSED at 4fde7462c (bazelisk test, 63 checks), cases 'a dry run warns that the npm environment is missing, with the steps to make it', 'preflight refuses a release with no npm environment', 'an npm environment open to every branch', 'an npm environment for another branch'. Creating the environment remains the owner's repository setting.","supersedes":"d8862507094b924f83798d71c52fd21afc4efebf7e999671e0316e185dae4882","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":".github/workflows/publish-pi.yml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:21:06.139262Z","id":"bb41302c29ca205ee4149bc8fd3baffa8aecc59b536a3bacb31aefbb33e79968","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:5b6825592","summary":"publish-pi.yml reads the conclusion of ci.yml's bazel job (gh run view --json jobs), and release.sh's step 13 waits for that job alone (ci_gate_state), not perf-log. Evidence: //scripts:release_script PASSED at 4fde7462c; its fake gh reports run 201 as 'completed cancelled' as a whole, and the full-run and resume cases pass on the bazel job's state.","supersedes":"f98bbcc12e690b22ab75a2ab1ca1b48e45c5d5016f01b899fad51d373251f7de","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":".github/workflows/ci.yml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T20:43:54.594941Z","id":"a76e764550eac739046557ad760f5fd11dd48130bbe72fec210d1f3c487747d0","body":{"detail":"Why the native tests and clippy stay outside Bazel too is the alternative recorded on crates/clax-worker/BUILD.bazel:1:35.","kind":"comment","references":"38985b9c78838e41be333a059185193c8479f029c7b59b504b5f6175c8cad1cf","summary":"The Worker's format check is now under Bazel (//crates/clax-worker:rustfmt, crates/clax-worker/BUILD.bazel); its tests, clippy, wasm build and e2e stay in the worker job (scripts/worker-checks.sh), as this alternative describes.","tags":["session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":".github/workflows/release.yml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T21:26:26.947222Z","id":"f24d6f3407afd12a98aa51bf9e80cdd5af84345e0765473756f59af03d7fb039","body":{"detail":"Every other build job runs on Blacksmith. Blacksmith offers no Intel Mac, and scripts/smoke-release-binary.sh runs the built binary, which on an arm64 Mac needs Rosetta; whether Blacksmith's macOS image has it is unverified. GitHub's macos-15-intel runs it natively.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":82},"end":{"line":82},"content_hash":"9ec025906e3aa3c5d0cdaf0a131e8bc14f37a7dab08dfd3e9e233a5c42d1026f"},"summary":"Build x86_64-apple-darwin on Blacksmith's arm64 Mac, cross-compiled, instead of GitHub's macos-15-intel","tags":["ci","release","revisit:Blacksmith offers an Intel Mac, or its arm64 macOS image is shown to run x86_64 binaries under Rosetta","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
